 be examined by a doctor...</div> </div> </div> </div>Doctor, Doctor Who?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12063-seta143","name":"Seta143","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-13T08:00:20-07:00","id":930845,"title":"","content":"The obvious reference here is, I think, Pinocchio. If you want to grow up, you've got to become a real boy.<br /> <br /> In other words, I agree with Dataweaver. For someone whose aspiration to humanity includes the goal of aging, physical maturation is an outcome of proceeding along the Pilgrimage. Maybe after a particularly dramatic story, the Promethean wakes up to discover she's grown half an inch, or sprouted a single very significant armpit hair.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12108-gscrap","name":"gscrap","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12108_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}